        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: auctōritās, auctōritātis",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "auctōritās, auctōritātis — \"authority, influence; backing\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Senex magnam auctōritātem in oppidō habet. The old man has great influence in the town."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "auctōritās, auctōritātis f. A man's weight in public life, earned by age and deeds. English authority."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "auctōritās is built on auctor \"a backer, an originator\" (EtymDB), which comes from augeō \"to increase\" (Lewis & Short). English authority comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
